  "asr_text": "I'm against a rule that makes phones off-limits even during breaks. I work at a warehouse during the day and go to evening high school at night, so I can't promise to cut off contact the whole time I'm at school. During breaks between classes, I get messages about changes to my shifts. If I reply late, the work goes to someone else. Once, my workplace kept calling during class. I couldn't answer, and later they told me it was a problem that they couldn't reach me. I almost had my shifts cut, too. I want to graduate from here. I also need money to give to my family. Now that I can follow my classes, I don't want to choose between work and school. I promise to keep my phone at the bottom of my bag and not touch it during class. But before you decide that phones are off-limits even during breaks, I want you to hear how I work, too.",
